native: apply INVERSE once (SGR 7), never also in the cell

OpenTUI 0.8.4 swaps fg/bg of an INVERSE cell in the buffer (buffer.zig, text-buffer drawing) AND keeps the INVERSE
bit, which the renderer writes as SGR 7: the terminal swaps a second time. With a background the inversion cancels;
with a transparent text background the swap makes fg = bg and the words disappear (the terminal Hub drew focused
rows as blank blocks). The cell now keeps the text's own colours and the terminal swaps once.
Kept SGR 7 (not "swap in the cell and clear the bit") because in mono mode (0004) SGR 7 is the only inversion there
is, and a transparent background then inverts against the terminal's own default background.
renderer.no-color.test.ts (0004) asserted the double-swapped colours; updated. New: renderer.inverse-once.test.ts.

